-- title:
--   H BConsistency Bad Mass Nonneg
-- statement:
--   **The interpolation bad mass is nonnegative.**
--
--   Let `params`, `strategy`, and `family` satisfy the field and positivity hypotheses, and fix a point $u$ and height tuple $x$. Every eligible-sandwich outcome operator and every vertical-line effect is positive semidefinite. Therefore the state-weighted bad mass satisfies
--
--   $$
--   0\le\mathsf{Bad}(u,x).
--   $$
--
--   This positivity is used when the bad mass is averaged over tuples and compared with the nonnegative consistency quantities.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.hBConsistencyBadMass_nonneg`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
